<refnamediv>
  <refname><type>SilikoValueStatus</type></refname>
  <refpurpose>Enumeration representing the status of a
    <type>SilikoValue</type></refpurpose>
</refnamediv>

<refsynopsisdiv>
<programlisting language="C">#include &lt;SilikoCore/Value.h&gt;</programlisting>

<programlisting language="C">enum SilikoValueStatus
{
    SilikoValueError = 0,
    SilikoValueInteger,
    SilikoValueReal
};</programlisting>
</refsynopsisdiv>

<refsection>
<title>Description</title>
<para>The <type>SilikoValueStatus</type> enumeration is used
to indicate whether an <type>SilikoValue</type> object is an integer
value, a real value, or an error.</para>
</refsection>

<refsection>
<title>Enumeration Values</title>

<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><literal>SilikoValueError</literal>: The value is an error.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><literal>SilikoValueInteger</literal>: The value is an integer.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para><literal>SilikoValueReal</literal>: The value is a real number.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</refsection>
